          "quote": "## Setup\n\n1. Put the warp in the center. Each player takes five planets of one color, places four of their twenty ships on each, and places their colony marker beside the warp's 0 space.\n2. Remove destiny cards naming unused player colors; shuffle the rest, including wilds and specials.\n3. Shuffle the flares, deal two to each player, and give them the matching alien sheets. Each secretly chooses one alien, initially placing it facedown, and returns the other sheet to the box. This is the standard selection procedure; Hidden Powers is a separate excluded variant. The original text does not specify when standard-game sheets are turned faceup; unlike the optional Hidden Powers rule, it gives no explicit reveal window. This source gap is recorded rather than supplying a new setup rule. Green/yellow/red indicate recommended experience, not strength. Beginners may start with green aliens without flares.\n4. Add **both flares dealt to every player**, including rejected aliens' flares, to the cosmic deck. Add random extras if needed to reach ten flares total; shuffle. Deal eight-card hands. Keep card faces private unless an effect allows showing them.\n5. Draw destiny until a player color appears; that player starts. Shuffle the drawn card back into the destiny deck. Play passes left thereafter.\n\nApply printed alien Game Setup instructions as well. If chosen aliens have a printed incompatibility, remove the alien bearing the restriction, keeping the unrestricted alien. Its player may use their originally rejected alien or draw a replacement unused flare and take that alien, redrawing conflicts. Gambler's printed restriction is **Do not use with Sorcerer**; using them together is an optional FAQ-permitted relaxation, outside this standard setup."
